IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Examinations and Assessment Board Act 2003 (Singapore) -- which examinations are "national" (s 2, Schedule), what the
-- Board must and may do (s 11), who sets the fees (s 12(1)(b), (c)), the old late charges validated (s 12A), the Board's board and
-- quorum (ss 5, 7, 9), protection from suit (s 17), and the offences: the Board's symbol (s 40), secrecy (s 41), corporate and
-- partnership liability (s 42), composition (s 43) and the penalty ceiling for regulations (s 45(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation marked
-- "version in force from 1/4/2024", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SEABA2003.txt. The latest amendment annotated is
-- "[Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024]" on s 12(1)(c) and s 12A; S 461/2020 and Act 5 of 2018 are also shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0209 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. Every family with a child at school meets the PSLE, N-, O- and A-Levels this Act names.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the common seal (s 4), delegation and committees (ss 6, 8, 14, 15), the chief executive and staff (s 16), finance
-- (ss 19-27), the 2004 transfer of property, employees, pensions, contracts and proceedings from the Examinations Division (ss 32-38),
-- and ministerial directions (s 13). No regulations made under s 45 were retrieved, so which offences are compoundable, and what the
-- fees are, is unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Examinations and Assessment Board Act 2003`

DECLARE Examination IS ONE OF
    `the PSLE`
    `the GCE O-Level`
    `the GCE N-Level`
    `the GCE A-Level`
    `a school's own mid-year test`
    `an aptitude test for a private employer`
    `the International Baccalaureate`

§§ `2 and Schedule -- national examinations and assessments`

-- s 2: "national examinations" means "the examinations specified in the Schedule". Schedule: 1. Primary School Leaving Examination
-- (PSLE); 2. Singapore-Cambridge GCE 'O'-Level; 3. 'N'-Level; 4. 'A'-Level. s 44: the Minister may amend the Schedule by Gazette.
-- "assessment" means "any test, examination or other method of assessing the level of proficiency, aptitude, skill, knowledge or
-- understanding of a person in any subject matter, OTHER THAN any of the national examinations".
GIVEN `the exam` IS AN Examination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a national examination` IF
    CONSIDER `the exam`
    WHEN `the PSLE` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the GCE O-Level` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the GCE N-Level` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the GCE A-Level` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the exam` IS AN Examination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an assessment` IF
    NOT `it is a national examination` `the exam`

§§ `11 -- what the Board must and may do`

-- s 11(1): the functions and duties of the Board are "(b) to organise and conduct the national examinations". (2)(a): the Board MAY,
-- "on terms that may be mutually agreed upon", "organise and conduct any assessment for or on behalf of the Government or any other
-- person or body in Singapore or elsewhere". (3): "Nothing in this section is to be construed as imposing on the Board, directly or
-- indirectly, any form of duty or liability enforceable by proceedings before any court to which it would not otherwise be subject."
GIVEN `the exam` IS AN Examination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board has a duty to conduct it` IF
    `it is a national examination` `the exam`

GIVEN `the exam` IS AN Examination, `terms are mutually agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may conduct it` IF
        `it is a national examination` `the exam`
    OR  (`it is an assessment` `the exam` AND `terms are mutually agreed`)

-- s 11(3) shuts out a suit founded on s 11 alone; any duty the Board "would otherwise be subject" to is untouched.
GIVEN `founded only on section 11` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Board would otherwise be liable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court claim against the Board can rest on it` IF
    `the Board would otherwise be liable` OR (NOT `founded only on section 11`)

§§ `12(1)(b), (c) and 12A -- fees and late charges`

-- s 12(1)(b): the Board may "determine, WITH THE APPROVAL OF THE MINISTER, and collect, the fees to be paid by candidates for any of
-- the national examinations"; (c) impose "(i) fees or commissions for services rendered by the Board, including the conduct of any
-- assessment ... and for the use of any facilities of the Board; and (ii) charges for the late payment of any such fee or commission".
-- Paragraph (c) mentions no ministerial approval. The late-payment charge in (c)(ii) attaches to "any SUCH fee or commission", that is
-- a (c)(i) fee: the text gives no late charge on a national-examination candidate fee under (b).
DECLARE Fee IS ONE OF
    `a candidate fee for a national examination`
    `a fee for conducting an assessment`
    `a fee for use of the Board's facilities`

GIVEN `the fee` IS A Fee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fee needs the Minister's approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the fee`
    WHEN `a candidate fee for a national examination` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the fee` IS A Fee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late-payment charge may be imposed on it under s 12(1)(c)(ii)` IF
    CONSIDER `the fee`
    WHEN `a candidate fee for a national examination` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 12A: "Every amount collected BEFORE the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or purportedly
-- as, a charge for the late payment of any fee or commission referred to in section 12(c) shall be deemed to be and always to have
-- been validly collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie". The deposit does not give that commencement date (the annotation reads
-- "wef 01/04/2024"), so it is a parameter here. Dates are written as YYYYMMDD numbers, which order as the dates do.
GIVEN `collected on` IS A NUMBER, `the 2008 Act commenced on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the late charge is validated and cannot be sued for` IF
    `collected on` LESS THAN `the 2008 Act commenced on`

§§ `5, 7 and 9 -- the Board, its terms and its quorum`

-- s 5(1): a Chairperson and "not less than 6 but not more than 9 other members", all appointed by the Minister. s 7(1): term "not
-- exceeding 3 years", re-appointment allowed; (3) revocation "without giving any reason". s 9(1): "a simple majority of the members
-- forms a quorum"; (4) majority of members present and voting; (5) Chairperson has a deliberative vote and a casting vote on equality.
-- Inference: "the members" for the quorum is read as the members in office (Chairperson included); the text does not say whether it
-- means the members in office or the full complement.
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is lawfully constituted in size` IF
    `other members` >= 6 AND `other members` <= 9

GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is within s 7(1)` IF
    `years` > 0 AND `years` <= 3

GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `members in office` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a quorum` IF
    `members present` * 2 > `members in office`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `presiding member votes for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is carried` IF
        `votes for` > `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` = `votes against` AND `presiding member votes for`)

§§ `17 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 17(1): no suit "shall lie personally against any member, officer or employee of the Board or other person acting under the
-- direction of the Board for anything which is IN GOOD FAITH done or intended to be done in the execution or purported execution of
-- this Act". (2): where the Board supplies information to the public "pursuant to any written law", neither the Board nor its people
-- are liable for loss "by reason of any error or omission ... if made in good faith and in the ordinary course of the discharge of the
-- duties". Note: (1) protects individuals personally; (2) also protects the Board itself, but only for information supplied pursuant to
-- written law.
GIVEN `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in executing the Act or other written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a personal suit against the officer is barred` IF
    `in good faith` AND `in executing the Act or other written law`

GIVEN `information supplied pursuant to written law` IS A BOOLEAN, `error made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the ordinary course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is shielded from the information error` IF
    `information supplied pursuant to written law` AND `error made in good faith` AND `in the ordinary course of duties`

§§ `40 -- the Board's symbol`

-- s 40(1): the Board "has the exclusive right to the use of such symbol or representation as the Board may select or devise". (2):
-- "Any person who uses a symbol or representation -- (a) identical with that of the Board; or (b) which so resembles that of the Board
-- as to deceive or cause confusion, or be likely to deceive or cause confusion, shall be guilty of an offence": fine up to $10,000 or
-- imprisonment up to 6 months or both. The subsection states no exception for use with the Board's consent and no mental element.
GIVEN `identical` IS A BOOLEAN, `likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence under s 40` IF
    `identical` OR `likely to deceive or confuse`

§§ `41 -- preservation of secrecy`

-- s 41(1): "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her duties or the exercise of his or her functions or when lawfully
-- required to do so by any court or where required or allowed by any written law, a person who is or HAS BEEN -- (a) a member, officer,
-- employee or agent of the Board; or (b) a member of a committee of the Board, must not disclose any information relating to the
-- affairs of the Board or of any other person" obtained in the performance of duties. (2): fine up to $2,000 or imprisonment up to
-- 24 months or both.
GIVEN `is or was a member, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obtained in performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed for duties` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disclosure is an offence under s 41` IF
        `is or was a member, officer, employee, agent or committee member`
    AND `obtained in performing duties`
    AND (NOT `disclosed for duties`)
    AND (NOT `required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `required or allowed by written law`)

§§ `40(2), 41(2), 43 and 45(3) -- penalties and composition`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misuse of the Board's symbol`
    `breach of secrecy`
    `contravention of regulations`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misuse of the Board's symbol` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breach of secrecy` THEN 2000
    WHEN `contravention of regulations` THEN 10000

-- Prison ceilings in months. s 45(3): regulations "may provide" a fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 12 months -- a ceiling on
-- what regulations may set, not a penalty the Act itself imposes.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misuse of the Board's symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `breach of secrecy` THEN 24
    WHEN `contravention of regulations` THEN 12

-- s 45(3): "in the case of a continuing offence, with a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which
-- the offence continues after conviction". A part of a day counts as a day, so `days after conviction` is a whole count.
GIVEN `days after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum fine for a continuing contravention of regulations` MEANS
    10000 + 1000 * `days after conviction`

-- s 43(1): "The chief executive or any officer authorised by the chief executive may compound any offence under this Act that is
-- PRESCRIBED as a compoundable offence by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum of money
-- not exceeding $1,000." (2): on payment "no further proceedings are to be taken". s 45(2)(d): the regulations prescribe which.
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `by the chief executive or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is valid` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `by the chief executive or an authorised officer` AND `sum` > 0 AND `sum` <= 1000

§§ `42 -- officers, partners and committee members`

-- s 42(1): an offence "committed by a body corporate ... with the consent or connivance of, or ... attributable to any neglect on the
-- part of, an officer" -- the officer as well as the body corporate is guilty. (3) the same for a partner of a partnership; (4) for "an
-- officer of the association or a member of its governing body" of an unincorporated association. (5): "officer" of a body corporate
-- means "a director, member of the committee of management, chief executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer ... or a
-- person purporting to act in any such capacity"; "partner" includes "a person purporting to act as a partner".
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a director`
    `a company secretary`
    `a person purporting to act as a manager`
    `a partner`
    `a person purporting to act as a partner`
    `the president of an association`
    `an ordinary shareholder`
    `a junior employee`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role is within s 42` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `an ordinary shareholder` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a junior employee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `the entity committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent, connivance or neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is also guilty` IF
    `the role is within s 42` `the role` AND `the entity committed the offence` AND `consent, connivance or neglect`
